  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    if not grid:\n        return []\n    \n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0]) if rows > 0 else 0\n    \n    # Find bounding box of all 5s\n    r_coords = []\n    c_coords = []\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[r][c] == 5:\n                r_coords.append(r)\n                c_coords.append(c)\n    \n    # If no 5s found, return copy as is\n    if not r_coords:\n        return [row[:] for row in grid]\n    \n    r_min, r_max = min(r_coords), max(r_coords)\n    c_min, c_max = min(c_coords), max(c_coords)\n    \n    # Identify all markers (non-0, non-5 values)\n    markers = []\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            val = grid[r][c]\n            if val != 0 and val != 5:\n                markers.append((r, c))\n    \n    # Create output grid as a deep copy\n    output = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    \n    # Clear all marker positions in output\n    for r, c in markers:\n        output[r][c] = 0\n    \n    # Project markers onto the boundary adjacent to the 5-block\n    for r, c in markers:\n        # Project vertically if above or below the 5-block\n        if r < r_min:\n            if r_min - 1 >= 0:\n                output[r_min - 1][c] = 5\n        elif r > r_max:\n            if r_max + 1 < rows:\n                output[r_max + 1][c] = 5\n        \n        # Project horizontally if left or right of the 5-block\n        if c < c_min:\n            if c_min - 1 >= 0:\n                output[r][c_min - 1] = 5\n        elif c > c_max:\n            if c_max + 1 < cols:\n                output[r][c_max + 1] = 5\n    \n    return output\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    if not grid:\n        return []\n    \n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0]) if rows > 0 else 0\n    \n    # Find bounding box of all 5s\n    r_coords = []\n    c_coords = []\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[r][c] == 5:\n                r_coords.append(r)\n                c_coords.append(c)\n    \n    # If no 5s found, return copy as is\n    if not r_coords:\n        return [row[:] for row in grid]\n    \n    r_min, r_max = min(r_coords), max(r_coords)\n    c_min, c_max = min(c_coords), max(c_coords)\n    \n    # Identify all markers (non-0, non-5 values)\n    markers = []\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            val = grid[r][c]\n            if val != 0 and val != 5:\n                markers.append((r, c))\n    \n    # Create output grid as a deep copy\n    output = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    \n    # Clear all marker positions in output\n    for r, c in markers:\n        output[r][c] = 0\n    \n    # Project markers onto the boundary adjacent to the 5-block\n    for r, c in markers:\n        # Project vertically if above or below the 5-block\n        if r < r_min:\n            if r_min - 1 >= 0:\n                output[r_min - 1][c] = 5\n        elif r > r_max:\n            if r_max + 1 < rows:\n                output[r_max + 1][c] = 5\n        \n        # Project horizontally if left or right of the 5-block\n        if c < c_min:\n            if c_min - 1 >= 0:\n                output[r][c_min - 1] = 5\n        elif c > c_max:\n            if c_max + 1 < cols:\n                output[r][c_max + 1] = 5\n    \n    return output",
